### Tested versions

Tested version was

Godot v4.5.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Ti Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7283) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-12900H (20 threads) - 31.71 GiB memory

Looking back through the versions of the code this issue has been there since the very first version of the http_request.cpp file.

### System information

Godot v4.5.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Ti Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7283) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-12900H (20 threads) - 31.71 GiB memory

### Issue description

## Expected behavior

A HTTP_Request's timeout of 5 seconds should be 5 seconds in real time not the engines internal adjusted time_scaled time.

## Current behavior

A HTTP_Request will adjust it's timeout by timescale so if timescale is 0.5 and the timeout is 5seconds it will timeout in 10 seconds and i time_scale is 0 it will never timeout.

## Cause

In http_request.cpp the timer constructed does not set the ignore_time_scale value to true so that timer is adjusted by the time_scale.

## Proposed solution

Set the ignore_time_scale=true on the newly constructed timer in the http_request constructor.

The solution to this would be to change the constructor in htt_request.cpp to

``` cpp

HTTPRequest::HTTPRequest() {
	client = Ref<HTTPClient>(HTTPClient::create());
	tls_options = TLSOptions::client();
	timer = memnew(Timer);
	timer->set_one_shot(true);
	timer->set_ignore_time_scale(true);
	timer->connect("timeout", callable_mp(this, &HTTPRequest::_timeout));
	add_child(timer);
}

```


### Steps to reproduce

If you use the example HTTP_Request code and add timeout=0.0001 without adjusting timescale it will timeout almost immediately. If you add time_scale=0 it will not timeout.

## With Timescale=1 Gives Timeout
``` gdscript
extends Node

func _ready():
	# Create an HTTP request node and connect its completion signal.
	var http_request = HTTPRequest.new()

	Engine.time_scale=0 # Leaving timsecale at 1
	http_request.timeout=0.0001 #Very short timeout

	add_child(http_request)
	http_request.request_completed.connect(self._http_request_completed)

	# Perform the HTTP request. The URL below returns a PNG image as of writing.
	var error = http_request.request("https://placehold.co/512.png")
	if error != OK:
		push_error("An error occurred in the HTTP request.")


# Called when the HTTP request is completed.
func _http_request_completed(result, response_code, headers, body):
	if result == HTTPRequest.RESULT_TIMEOUT:
		push_error("Download Timedout.")
		return

	if result != HTTPRequest.RESULT_SUCCESS:
		push_error("Image couldn't be downloaded. Try a different image.")
		return

	var image = Image.new()
	var error = image.load_png_from_buffer(body)
	if error != OK:
		push_error("Couldn't load the image.")

	var texture = ImageTexture.create_from_image(image)

	# Display the image in a TextureRect node.
	var texture_rect = TextureRect.new()
	add_child(texture_rect)
	texture_rect.texture = texture
```

When executing the above we get the following error.

```
E 0:00:05:065   test_timeout.gd:20 @ _http_request_completed(): Download Timedout.
  <C++ Source>  core/variant/variant_utility.cpp:1024 @ push_error()
  <Stack Trace> test_timeout.gd:20 @ _http_request_completed()
```

## With Timescale=0 does not give Timeout

``` gdscript
extends Node

func _ready():
	# Create an HTTP request node and connect its completion signal.
	var http_request = HTTPRequest.new()

	Engine.time_scale=0 # Setting timescale to 0
	http_request.timeout=0.0001 #Very short timeout

	add_child(http_request)
	http_request.request_completed.connect(self._http_request_completed)

	# Perform the HTTP request. The URL below returns a PNG image as of writing.
	var error = http_request.request("https://placehold.co/512.png")
	if error != OK:
		push_error("An error occurred in the HTTP request.")


# Called when the HTTP request is completed.
func _http_request_completed(result, response_code, headers, body):
	if result == HTTPRequest.RESULT_TIMEOUT:
		push_error("Download Timedout.")
		return

	if result != HTTPRequest.RESULT_SUCCESS:
		push_error("Image couldn't be downloaded. Try a different image.")
		return

	var image = Image.new()
	var error = image.load_png_from_buffer(body)
	if error != OK:
		push_error("Couldn't load the image.")

	var texture = ImageTexture.create_from_image(image)

	# Display the image in a TextureRect node.
	var texture_rect = TextureRect.new()
	add_child(texture_rect)
	texture_rect.texture = texture
```

With the `time_scale=0` the image loads and no error is shown.


